---
import banner from '../../content/blog/using-dspy/banner.png';
// Bench objects: Plate and Fan. Covers come from src/assets/covers via coverFor; glow from glowOf.
import { coverFor } from '../../utils/covers';
import { glowOf } from '../../utils/glow';
import Fan from '../ui/Fan.astro';
import FanItem from '../ui/FanItem.astro';
import Label from '../ui/Label.astro';
import Plate from '../ui/Plate.astro';
import PostCard from '../ui/PostCard.astro';

const eden = coverFor('9780143129486');
const dalio = coverFor('9781982160272');
const edenGlow = eden ? await glowOf(eden) : undefined;
const dalioGlow = dalio ? await glowOf(dalio) : undefined;
---

<section class="objects" aria-labelledby="objects-h">
	<Label as="h2" id="objects-h">Objects</Label>

	<div class="group">
		<Label as="h3">Plate</Label>
		<div class="row">
			<figure><Plate src={eden} alt="East of Eden cover" /><figcaption>image</figcaption></figure>
			<figure><Plate src={eden} alt="East of Eden cover" glow={edenGlow} /><figcaption>glow</figcaption></figure>
			<figure><Plate src={dalio} alt="Changing World Order cover" glow={dalioGlow} ratio="1/1" radius="md" /><figcaption>1/1, radius md</figcaption></figure>
			<figure>
				<Plate>
					<span class="type"><strong>East of Eden</strong><span>John Steinbeck</span></span>
				</Plate>
				<figcaption>typographic</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
		<p class="note">
			One physical object: --elevation-object, a 1px inner hairline, a fixed ratio. glow is a colour sampled from the
			image at build time (glowOf), the one coloured halo; a parent raises it with --plate-glow-strength and swaps the
			shadow with --plate-shadow.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="group">
		<Label as="h3">Fan</Label>
		<Fan class="demo">
			<FanItem i={0} rest={{ r: 0 }} open={{ x: '30%', r: 8, s: 1.02 }} touch={{ x: '10%', r: 4 }}>
				<Plate src={eden} alt="East of Eden cover" glow={edenGlow} />
			</FanItem>
			<FanItem i={1} rest={{ x: '8%', y: '-3%', r: -5 }} open={{ x: '-8%', y: '-6%', r: -6 }} touch={{ x: '-4%', y: '-3%', r: -5 }}>
				<Plate src={dalio} alt="Changing World Order cover" glow={dalioGlow} />
			</FanItem>
			<FanItem i={2} rest={{ x: '14%', y: '-5%', r: 5 }} open={{ x: '-50%', y: '-4%', r: -16 }} touch={{ x: '-30%', y: '-4%', r: -12 }}>
				<Plate><span class="type"><strong>Third</strong><span>Typographic</span></span></Plate>
			</FanItem>
		</Fan>
		<p class="note">
			Hover or focus inside the Fan (host "self"), or an ancestor with data-fan-host (host "ancestor"). Item 0 is the
			front. Each FanItem takes rest, open and touch poses {"{"} x, y, r, s {"}"}; enter is --duration-moderate with
			--ease-spring and 40ms stagger, exit --duration-base. Once open, the card under the pointer or focus rises to the top, straightens, grows and lifts while its siblings recede, with no stagger; reduced motion keeps only the z-index raise and the shadow change.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="group">
		<Label as="h3">PostCard</Label>
		<div class="row cards">
			<figure>
				<PostCard href="#" title="Using DSPy" description="Programming rather than prompting a language model." date={new Date('2025-03-02')} image={banner} />
				<figcaption>image</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<figure>
				<PostCard href="#" title="A post without a banner image" description="The title is set large on the card instead." date={new Date('2024-11-20')} />
				<figcaption>typographic</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<figure>
				<PostCard href="#" title="Using DSPy" description="Programming rather than prompting a language model." date={new Date('2025-03-02')} image={banner} size="sm" />
				<figcaption>size sm</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
		<p class="note">
			One link, one index card: the card is the shadowed object (--plate-shadow, so a Fan lifts it) and its Plate gives
			up its own shadow. Banner on top, or the title set large with a mono date; then title and description, each
			clamped. bannerFor(post) finds a post's banner.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.objects {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-10);
	}
	.group {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		padding: var(--pad-tile);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius-tile);
		background: var(--surface);
		color: var(--surface-foreground);
	}
	.row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(8rem, 10rem));
		gap: var(--space-8);
	}
	figure {
		margin: 0;
	}
	figcaption {
		margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
	}
	.group :global(.demo) {
		--fan-w: 9rem;
		margin: var(--space-6) var(--space-16) var(--space-6) var(--space-16);
	}
	.type {
		display: grid;
		align-content: end;
		gap: var(--space-1);
		height: 100%;
		padding: var(--space-3);
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
	}
	.type strong {
		color: var(--foreground);
		font-weight: var(--weight-title);
	}
	.cards {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(12rem, 15rem));
	}
	.note {
		max-width: 48rem;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		line-height: var(--leading-ui);
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
	}
</style>
